# Cup Test - TCUP, a TEST course (SPEC.md 137.54.2): the BZDEV=1 build's alone, after the shipped courses (the
# Makefile's BZ_TESTCRS), on no pad, with no shipped demo.  TQUIK's partner for "exits and the save"
# (docs/plans/BOUNCE-BONANZA-SOAK.md): a course finishes at GOAL cells or in a CUP, never both (SPEC.md
# 137.14.4.1), so the cup's way out is a course of its own -
#  - a start plate, a ramp down along +x and a foot with the CUP on the route: the autopilot holes out in
#    291 steps (5.3 s), no fall (the cup's exit, a second course's best);
#  - the STEEL ball (TQUIK's is rubber: the two roll two materials) and the default palette (30h, the BIOS's:
#    the palette leg's second course beside TQUIK's 10h); the tool's limit; the finish clock beside the foot.
course TCUP "Cup Test"
test             # SPEC.md 137.54: a test course - no pad, no shipped demo, no target owed
music fairway    # SPEC.md 137.50.3: every course names its song
width 64
ball steel
floor rect   3 4  7 7  flat 4             # the start plate
wall  rect   3 3  7 4  flat 6             # its back rail
floor rect   7 4 11 7  ramp x 7 11 4 2    # the ramp, down along +x
floor rect  11 4 15 7  flat 2             # the foot
cup 13 5                                  # the finish
start 4 5
way 4 5
way 13 5
clock 11 6                                # the finish clock (SPEC.md 137.22.6)
